# The raw NSE files ARE committed, deliberately.
#
# They are 86 MB and grow about 21 MB a year -- unremarkable for GitHub,
# whose soft limit is 1 GB. In exchange, the weekly job in CI can rebuild
# every number from scratch and check the nightly shortcut has not drifted.
# Without them that check is impossible, and an unattended nightly update
# nobody can verify is worse than no automation at all.
#
# They are excluded from the Docker image by .dockerignore: the running site
# reads the computed CSVs and never opens a bhavcopy.

# Source PDFs stay local. rag.py has already turned them into
# data/chunks.json, which is all the deployed site needs.
docs/*.pdf

# Secrets
.env

# C++ build output
cpp/libiv.so
cpp/libiv.dll
*.o

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
